==Grammar==
The Selkʼnam language is an [[Object–verb–subject|object–verb–subject language]] (OVS). This is a rare [[word order]]: only 1% of languages use it as their default word order. There are only two word classes in Selkʼnam: nouns and verbs.<ref>{{cite book |last=Najlis |first=Elena L. |title=Lengua selknam |year=1973 |publisher=[[Universidad de Salvador]] |location=Buenos Aires |series=Filología y lingüística |volume=3 |language=es}}</ref>

== Vocabulary ==
The Selkʼnam language has Chonan vocabulary similar to the [[Haush language]], though some words have been adopted from [[Spanish language|Spanish]] and [[English language|English]], such as the word for {{gloss|cat}}, in Selkʼnam, {{lang|ona|kʼlattítaŭ}}; from the Spanish word {{lang|es|gatito}}, which translates to {{gloss|kitten}}.<ref>{{Cite book |last=Lehmann-Nitsche |first=Roberto |title=Selkʼnam words. The Ōōna vocabulary collected by Roberto Lehmann-Nitsche |year=1913}}</ref>

